			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Introduce comprehensive architecture documentation\n\nCreate `Documentation/GitHub/Architecture.md` to serve as the definitive technical reference for the Mountain native backend. This document details the Tauri-based application lifecycle, the implementation of Common traits via the `MountainEnvironment` provider system, and the orchestration of sidecar processes (Cocoon, Air).\n\nThe narrative covers critical subsystems including the gRPC server (Vine) for inter-process communication, the Tauri command registration system, state management via `AppState`, and the process management strategies for extension hosts and background daemons. It also catalogs the IPC event system and caching mechanisms.\n\nThis addition provides necessary context for developers and auditors regarding the Rust backend's structure, effectively replacing scattered code comments with a structured, high-level overview of the editor's native substrate.",
			"SHA": "d4d6944bdecaae78a45ed256e1a6288488f5056d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-15T21:32:29Z",
